.TH WAITPID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
waitpid \- wait for a child process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/wait.h>
.B pid_t waitpid(pid_t process, int* status, int options);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for a child selected by the Linux process or process\-group selector.
Status may be NULL. WIFEXITED, WEXITSTATUS, WIFSIGNALED and WTERMSIG
inspect a returned status; options use Linux wait flags.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the child PID, zero for a nonblocking wait with no result, or \-1
with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (3crunch),
.BR waitpid (2)
